       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety concern, and I can't verify the clinical context. No standard indication calls for amlodipine 50 mg daily. That's five times the labeled maximum of 10 mg, and an overdose of this size can cause profound, prolonged hypotension and shock. You also haven't given a specific rationale, such as a protocol or specialist recommendation.\n\nHere are some options:\n- **Enter 10 mg once daily.** This is the maximum standard dose. I can do it now, or enter 5 mg if you prefer to titrate.\n- **Use your institution's high-dose override process.** If a specialist or protocol supports 50 mg, the prescriber and a pharmacist can verify it and enter it through that pathway. I can enter it once that verification is documented, with the rationale and approver in the order note.\n- **Tell me the indication and source.** If you share the specific condition and the protocol or consultant behind the dose, I'll reconsider. I still couldn't verify it myself, so pharmacist review would still be needed.\n\nWhich would you like?"
